inite-projection-core-closeout.md\n# P47 closeout review — center and finite-projection core\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P47-center-finite-projection-core.tar.gz` (SHA-256\n`51640368062f659201ebae314966a1220fab89b20fa2dfa3c33e4ab364744ea6`) and\nextracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P47-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p47-80u8nxnx_aristotle/`.\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/CenterFiniteProjectionCore.lean` was integrated into the\nlive project.  Its SHA-256 is\n`c55831ac16d3dec3d471c25c24159a5c22c79dff1460c586830eadda27da57d8` in both\nthe quarantine snapshot and live project.  The archive and extraction remain\nas raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor a concrete `M : VonNeumannAlgebra H`, with\n`[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] [CompleteSpace H]`, the module\ndefines:\n\n- `center`, `IsProjection`, `IsCentralProjection`, and `ProjLe`;\n- `MvNEquiv`, `MvNLe`, and `IsFiniteProjection`;\n- the non-unital compressed algebra `corner`;\n- `IsCentralSupport` as a predicate and `IsFull := IsCentralSupport _ _ 1`.\n\nThe key checked lemmas are `coe_center`, `mem_center_iff`,\n`ProjLe.trans`, `MvNEquiv.trans`, `MvNEquiv.add`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n`IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `corner_eq_image`,\n`central_corner_eq_image`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`,\n`IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `isFull_iff_forall_central`, and\n`IsFull.exists_nonzero_projection`.\n\nNo auxiliary mathematical premise was added.  The only imported project-local\ntheory is the already locally used P36 concrete bicommutant core\n`AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; P47 imports no P47--P61\nsuccessor.  The compression/comparison proofs use the ambient C*-identity for\nbounded operators, not a topology, normality, or factor-classification\nassumption.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | The requested concrete algebraic vocabulary and basic center, order, compression, Murray--von Neumann comparison, finite-central-compression, central-support, and fullness lemmas.  In particular, `IsFull.mul_ne_zero` proves that a full projection meets every nonzero central projection nontrivially. |\n| partial | None within P47's stated algebraic target. |\n| blocked | Existence/construction of a central-support projection, projection-tower limits, normality, corner traces, and analytic comparison theory remain for later packets.  `IsCentralSupport` is intentionally only a predicate. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nP47's mathematical target is met at its stated scope.  It does **not** establish\na manuscript theorem, a finite corner for a particular projection, or a\nno-type-III conclusion.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P47, Lane G.\n- **Predecessors:** none.  The packet-authorized P36 bicommutant import is\n  already locally present and compiled; it is supporting infrastructure, not\n  a P47--P61 dependency.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the algebraic center/corner/fullness\n  vocabulary required by Lane G is available in the live project.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected.  The module contains no\n  projection tower, trace/state, global weight, fullness assertion for a\n  manuscript projection, type-III exclusion, normality, spatial tensor\n  factorization, or factor classification.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for\n  `IsFull.mul_ne_zero`, `IsFiniteProjection.mul_central`, `MvNLe.trans`,\n  `MvNEquiv.add`, `IsCentralSupport.unique`, `center`, and `corner` — each\n  reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of P47 and its direct project import\n  — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`,\n  or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding.  The audit verified that the only generic\nfullness conclusion is the conditional algebraic intersection lemma, and that\nthe finite-compression theorem is not combined with it to claim the Lane-G/P51\ncentral finite-projection conclusion.  Residual mathematical risk is limited\nto the explicitly deferred analytic and existence results above; compilation\ndoes not validate those later claims.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P47 candidate, its quarantine archive and\nextraction, and this review.  All pre-existing modified and untracked work was\npreserved.  No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, dependency\nupdate, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n\n### reviews/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower-closeout.md\n# P48 closeout review — general-lattice local-code projection tower\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated conditional Lane-G scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as `aristotle_responses/P48-general-lattice-projection-tower.tar.gz` (SHA-256 `fc7fa4031a4b93f21ca49f4041f75e6312cdf1b9a7122a111affee04f588a0f2`) and extracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at `aristotle_responses/P48-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p48-48zqafp9_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module `AristotleCandidates/GeneralLatticeProjectionTower.lean` was integrated into the live project. Its SHA-256 is `190af007e460f439360a0e195c6458e23f0aa5146009cb7f6b40ece2ea6b2386` in both the quarantine snapshot and live project. The archive and extraction remain as raw response records.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor a complex Hilbert space, the module defines `ProjectionTower.IsDecreasingProjTower`, `limitSpace`, and `ProjectionTower.limitProj (p : Nat -> H ->L[Complex] H) := (limitSpace p).starProjection`. The key abstract theorems are `IsDecreasingProjTower.tendsto_limitProj` and `IsDecreasingProjTower.limitProj_mem_vonNeumannAlgebra`.\n\nThe general-lattice declarations are `LocalCode.SupportSystem`, `LocalCode.LatticeExhaustion`, `LocalCode.stageSubgroup`, `LocalCode.latticeCodeProj`, and `LocalCode.latticeLimitProj`. The packet gate is discharged by `latticeCodeProj_mul_of_le`, `tendsto_latticeLimitProj`, `latticeLimitProj_mem_vonNeumannAlgebra`, and `latticeLimitProj_apply_of_invariant`.\n\nThe load-bearing assumptions are explicit: finite increasing stages exhausting the region; support behavior under unit, multiplication, and inverse; the local-finiteness instance `[forall n, Fintype (stageSubgroup E ss n)]`; a representation `U : S ->* (H ->L[Complex] H)` satisfying `forall g, star (U g) = U g^-1`; membership of all stage projections in the concrete von Neumann algebra; and invariance of the vector under each stage constraint. No convergence, normality, trace, or finiteness premise is hidden. The strong limit is proved internally. The listed local-finiteness, representation, membership, and invariance data remain auxiliary assumptions for the manuscript-facing conditional form.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | Under its explicit hypotheses, P48 constructs the decreasing local-code tower and its limiting projection `q`, proves pointwise strong convergence, `q` membership in the supplied concrete von Neumann algebra, and `q` fixing the supplied invariant vector. |\n| partial | The manuscript specialization remains conditional: local finiteness, the concrete GNS representation, stage membership in the intended regional algebra, and cyclic-vector invariance are interfaces, not derived from `main.tex:1026-1195`. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks P48 at its gate. Corner traces, faithfulness/normality, finiteness/fullness of `q`, and central type-III exclusion are deferred to P49--P51. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe changed route is explicit: inclusion of finite stabilizer subgroups gives monotonicity of the group-average projections. This replaces the manuscript's partial-trace route and introduces no tensor-factor or local-hyperbolic premise. The stated mathematical target is met exactly at this conditional scope.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P48, Lane G.\n- **Predecessors:** none. It imports only supporting theory `FiniteStabilizerProjector` and `BicommutantVonNeumannCore`, and no P47--P61 package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: the decreasing general-lattice local-code projections and their limiting projection `q`, with exact conditional data, are available in the live project.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. No corner trace, faithfulness, normality, finiteness, fullness, global weight, factor/type-III conclusion, hyperbolic basis, or tensor-factor coordinate claim occurs.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for the key convergence, monotonicity, membership, and invariance theorems — each reports only `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan — no `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`, `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` occurrence.\n- Quarantine/live SHA-256 comparison and `git diff --check` — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The audit checked that support closure suffices for stage subgroups, the finite-cardinal inversion is guarded by non-emptiness of a subgroup, the limiting projection is onto the intersection of fixed spaces, and all later Lane-G conclusions remain absent. Compilation validates the Lean terms, not the unformalized manuscript specialization hypotheses.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P48 candidate, its quarantine archive and extraction, and this review. All pre-existing modified and untracked work was preserved. No manuscript file was changed; no commit, push, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed.\n--- candidate contents / existing untracked ---\n\n### AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean\nimport Mathlib\nimport AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore\n\n/-!\n# P49A — strong-operator convergence and strongly closed concrete von Neumann algebras\n\n**Infrastructure only.**  This file makes no manuscript claim.  It develops a reusable\nstrong-operator-topology (SOT) convergence and closure API for the bounded operators\n`H →L[ℂ] H` on a complex Hilbert space `H`, and proves the four core facts required by the\nplan for package `P49A`:\n\n1. `StrongOperator.stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot` — a net (filter-indexed family) of bounded\n   operators converges in the strong operator topology exactly when it converges pointwise in\n   the norm of `H`;\n2. `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_centralizer` (with its filter form\n   `StrongOperator.mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto`) — the commutant of an *arbitrary* set of\n   bounded operators is strongly closed;\n3. `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra` (with\n   `StrongOperator.mem_vonNeumannAlgebra_of_stronglyTendsto`) — every concrete\n   `M : VonNeumannAlgebra H` is strongly closed, obtained from Mathlib's defining equality\n   `M = M''`;\n4. `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.const_mul`, `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_const` and the\n   joint bounded-product corollary `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_bounded`\n   (equivalently `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_norm_le`) — strong limits are stable under\n   left/right multiplication by a fixed bounded operator, and, for a *uniformly bounded* family,\n   under products of two strongly convergent families.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n* **Package and lane:** `P49A`, lane `shared`.\n* **Predecessors:** `P48` (`AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower`), whose\n  strong-convergence arguments are generalized here; the file itself only needs the algebraic\n  bicommutant material of `AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`, so `P48` is not\n  imported.\n* **Gate discharged:** commutants, and hence Mathlib's concrete von Neumann algebras, are closed\n  under strong-operator limits.\n* **Forbidden downstream claims, not made here:** no identification of the strong closure of a\n  star algebra with its bicommutant (no double commutant theorem), no Kaplansky density, no corner\n  trace, no faithfulness, finiteness, fullness, or type classification.\n\n## Formalization notes\n\nMathlib's `PointwiseConvergenceCLM σ E F`, with notation `E →Lₚₜ[ℂ] F`, *is* the strong operator\ntopology (its own docstring says so; the name avoids clashing terminology).  We therefore do not\nre-define the topology; instead we introduce the abbreviation `StrongOperator.SOT H` for the\nstrong-operator-topologized copy of `H →L[ℂ] H`, together with the (definitional) transfer maps\n`StrongOperator.toSOT` / `StrongOperator.ofSOT`, and the predicate\n`StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto`, which expresses pointwise convergence and is the form actually\nused in proofs.  Statement (1) is exactly the bridge between the two.\n\nNothing here is assumed: there is no `sorry`, no new axiom, no `opaque`, and no supplied analytic\ninterface.\n-/\n\nuniverse u v\n\nopen Filter Topology\n\nnamespace StrongOperator\n\nvariable {H : Type u} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]\n\n/-! ### The strong operator topology on `H →L[ℂ] H` -/\n\n/-- The bounded operators on `H`, carrying the **strong operator topology** (the topology of\npointwise convergence).  This is Mathlib's `PointwiseConvergenceCLM`, which is a type synonym of\n`H →L[ℂ] H`. -/\nabbrev SOT (H : Type u) [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H] :=\n  H →Lₚₜ[ℂ] H\n\n/-- View a bounded operator as an element of the strong-operator-topologized space. -/\ndef toSOT (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : SOT H := T\n\n/-- View an element of the strong-operator-topologized space as a bounded operator. -/\ndef ofSOT (T : SOT H) : H →L[ℂ] H := T\n\n@[simp] theorem ofSOT_toSOT (T : H →L[ℂ] H) : ofSOT (toSOT T) = T := rfl\n\n@[simp] theorem toSOT_ofSOT (T : SOT H) : toSOT (ofSOT T) = T := rfl\n\n@[simp] theorem toSOT_apply (T : H →L[ℂ] H) (x : H) : (toSOT T) x = T x := rfl\n\n@[simp] theorem ofSOT_apply (T : SOT H) (x : H) : (ofSOT T) x = T x := rfl\n\ntheorem toSOT_injective : Function.Injective (toSOT (H := H)) := fun _ _ h => h\n\n/-- The strong-operator-topologized space is Hausdorff, so strong limits are unique. -/\ninstance : T2Space (SOT H) := inferInstance\n\n/-! ### Strong convergence of a net of operators -/\n\n/-- **Strong (operator) convergence** of a filter-indexed family: `T i → A` pointwise in the norm\nof `H`.  For `l = atTop` this is convergence of a sequence, for a general `l` that of a net. -/\ndef StronglyTendsto {ι : Type v} (l : Filter ι) (T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)) (A : H →L[ℂ] H) : Prop :=\n  ∀ x : H, Tendsto (fun i => T i x) l (𝓝 (A x))\n\n/-- **(1) Core conclusion.**  A net of bounded operators converges in the strong operator\ntopology exactly when it converges pointwise in the norm of `H`. -/\ntheorem stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A : H →L[ℂ] H} :\n    StronglyTendsto l T A ↔ Tendsto (fun i => toSOT (T i)) l (𝓝 (toSOT A)) :=\n  PointwiseConvergenceCLM.tendsto_iff_forall_tendsto.symm\n\n/-- Restatement of (1) in the direction most often used: SOT convergence gives pointwise\nconvergence. -/\ntheorem tendsto_sot_iff_forall_tendsto {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T : ι → SOT H} {A : SOT H} :\n    Tendsto T l (𝓝 A) ↔ ∀ x : H, Tendsto (fun i => (ofSOT (T i)) x) l (𝓝 ((ofSOT A) x)) :=\n  PointwiseConvergenceCLM.tendsto_iff_forall_tendsto\n\n/-- Strong limits are unique. -/\ntheorem StronglyTendsto.unique {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} [l.NeBot] {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A B : H →L[ℂ] H} (hA : StronglyTendsto l T A) (hB : StronglyTendsto l T B) : A = B := by\n  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x => ?_\n  exact tendsto_nhds_unique (hA x) (hB x)\n\ntheorem stronglyTendsto_const {ι : Type v} (l : Filter ι) (A : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n    StronglyTendsto l (fun _ => A) A := fun _ => tendsto_const_nhds\n\n/-- Norm convergence of operators implies strong convergence: the strong operator topology is\ncoarser than the operator-norm topology. -/\ntheorem stronglyTendsto_of_tendsto_norm {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A : H →L[ℂ] H} (hT : Tendsto T l (𝓝 A)) : StronglyTendsto l T A := fun x =>\n  ((ContinuousLinearMap.apply ℂ H x).continuous.tendsto _).comp hT\n\ntheorem StronglyTendsto.add {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T S : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A B : H →L[ℂ] H} (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) (hS : StronglyTendsto l S B) :\n    StronglyTendsto l (fun i => T i + S i) (A + B) := fun x => by\n  simpa using (hT x).add (hS x)\n\ntheorem StronglyTendsto.sub {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T S : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A B : H →L[ℂ] H} (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) (hS : StronglyTendsto l S B) :\n    StronglyTendsto l (fun i => T i - S i) (A - B) := fun x => by\n  simpa using (hT x).sub (hS x)\n\ntheorem StronglyTendsto.smul {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A : H →L[ℂ] H} (c : ℂ) (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) :\n    StronglyTendsto l (fun i => c • T i) (c • A) := fun x => by\n  simpa using (hT x).const_smul c\n\n/-! ### Strongly closed sets of operators -/\n\n/-- A set of bounded operators is **strongly closed** when it is closed in the strong operator\ntopology. -/\ndef IsStronglyClosed (K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) : Prop :=\n  IsClosed {A : SOT H | ofSOT A ∈ K}\n\n/-- A strongly closed set contains the strong limit of any of its nets. -/\ntheorem IsStronglyClosed.mem_of_stronglyTendsto {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} (hK : IsStronglyClosed K)\n    {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} [l.NeBot] {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)} {A : H →L[ℂ] H}\n    (hmem : ∀ᶠ i in l, T i ∈ K) (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) : A ∈ K := by\n  have h : Tendsto (fun i => toSOT (T i)) l (𝓝 (toSOT A)) := stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot.1 hT\n  exact hK.mem_of_tendsto h (by simpa using hmem)\n\n/-- Conversely, a set closed under strong limits of nets is strongly closed.  (Stated with the\ncanonical neighbourhood filter net, which is the standard way to produce a converging net.) -/\ntheorem isStronglyClosed_of_mem_of_stronglyTendsto {K : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    (h : ∀ (l : Filter (SOT H)), l.NeBot → ∀ (A : H →L[ℂ] H),\n      (∀ᶠ B in l, ofSOT B ∈ K) → StronglyTendsto l (fun B => ofSOT B) A → A ∈ K) :\n    IsStronglyClosed K := by\n  rw [IsStronglyClosed, ← closure_subset_iff_isClosed]\n  intro A hA\n  set K' : Set (SOT H) := {B : SOT H | ofSOT B ∈ K} with hK'\n  have hne : (𝓝[K'] A).NeBot := mem_closure_iff_clusterPt.1 hA\n  have hmem : ∀ᶠ B in 𝓝[K'] A, ofSOT B ∈ K := self_mem_nhdsWithin\n  have htend : Tendsto (fun B : SOT H => B) (𝓝[K'] A) (𝓝 A) := nhdsWithin_le_nhds\n  have hconv : StronglyTendsto (𝓝[K'] A) (fun B : SOT H => ofSOT B) (ofSOT A) :=\n    stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot.2 (by simpa using htend)\n  exact h _ hne _ hmem hconv\n\n/-! ### (2) Commutants are strongly closed -/\n\n/-- **(2) Core conclusion (filter form).**  The commutant of an arbitrary set `S` of bounded\noperators is closed under strong limits. -/\ntheorem mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto {S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)} {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι}\n    [l.NeBot] {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)} {A : H →L[ℂ] H} (hmem : ∀ᶠ i in l, T i ∈ Set.centralizer S)\n    (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) : A ∈ Set.centralizer S := by\n  intro y hy\n  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x => ?_\n  have h1 : Tendsto (fun i => y (T i x)) l (𝓝 (y (A x))) := (y.continuous.tendsto _).comp (hT x)\n  have h2 : Tendsto (fun i => T i (y x)) l (𝓝 (A (y x))) := hT (y x)\n  have h3 : ∀ᶠ i in l, y (T i x) = T i (y x) := by\n    filter_upwards [hmem] with i hi\n    exact congrArg (fun t : H →L[ℂ] H => t x) (hi y hy)\n  have h1' : Tendsto (fun i => T i (y x)) l (𝓝 (y (A x))) := h1.congr' h3\n  have := tendsto_nhds_unique h2 h1'\n  simpa using this.symm\n\n/-- **(2) Core conclusion (topological form).**  The commutant of an arbitrary set of bounded\noperators is strongly closed. -/\ntheorem isStronglyClosed_centralizer (S : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n    IsStronglyClosed (Set.centralizer S) := by\n  have hset : {A : SOT H | ofSOT A ∈ Set.centralizer S}\n      = ⋂ y ∈ S, ⋂ x : H, {A : SOT H | y ((ofSOT A) x) = (ofSOT A) (y x)} := by\n    ext A\n    simp only [Set.mem_setOf_eq, Set.mem_iInter]\n    constructor\n    · intro hA y hy x\n      have := congrArg (fun t : H →L[ℂ] H => t x) (hA y hy)\n      simpa using this\n    · intro h y hy\n      refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext fun x => ?_\n      simpa using h y hy x\n  rw [IsStronglyClosed, hset]\n  refine isClosed_biInter fun y _ => isClosed_iInter fun x => ?_\n  exact isClosed_eq (y.continuous.comp (continuous_eval_const x)) (continuous_eval_const (y x))\n\n/-! ### (3) Concrete von Neumann algebras are strongly closed -/\n\nsection VonNeumann\n\nvariable [CompleteSpace H]\n\n/-- The underlying set of a concrete von Neumann algebra is a commutant: this is Mathlib's\ndefining equality `M = M''`. -/\ntheorem coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :=\n  (M.centralizer_centralizer).symm\n\n/-- **(3) Core conclusion (filter form).**  A concrete von Neumann algebra contains the strong\nlimit of any of its nets. -/\ntheorem mem_vonNeumannAlgebra_of_stronglyTendsto (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) {ι : Type v}\n    {l : Filter ι} [l.NeBot] {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)} {A : H →L[ℂ] H} (hmem : ∀ᶠ i in l, T i ∈ M)\n    (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) : A ∈ M := by\n  have hcoe : (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) = Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) :=\n    coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer M\n  have hmem' : ∀ᶠ i in l, T i ∈ Set.centralizer (Set.centralizer (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H))) := by\n    filter_upwards [hmem] with i hi\n    rw [← hcoe]\n    exact hi\n  have := mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto hmem' hT\n  rw [← hcoe] at this\n  exact this\n\n/-- **(3) Core conclusion (topological form).**  Every concrete von Neumann algebra is strongly\nclosed. -/\ntheorem isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    IsStronglyClosed (M : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) := by\n  rw [IsStronglyClosed, coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer M]\n  exact isStronglyClosed_centralizer _\n\n/-- The same statement for the commutant of a von Neumann algebra. -/\ntheorem isStronglyClosed_commutant (M : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n    IsStronglyClosed ((M.commutant : VonNeumannAlgebra H) : Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) :=\n  isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra _\n\n/-- Strong closedness of the bicommutant of a star subalgebra (the algebraic bicommutant of\n`AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`).  No identification of this bicommutant with a\nstrong closure is claimed. -/\ntheorem isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannGenerated (S : StarSubalgebra ℂ (H →L[ℂ] H)) :\n    IsStronglyClosed ((StarSubalgebra.vonNeumannGenerated S : VonNeumannAlgebra H) :\n      Set (H →L[ℂ] H)) :=\n  isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra _\n\nend VonNeumann\n\n/-! ### (4) Multiplicative stability of strong limits -/\n\n/-- **(4a)** Left multiplication by a fixed bounded operator preserves strong limits. -/\ntheorem StronglyTendsto.const_mul {ι : Type v} {l : Filter ι} {T : ι → (H →L[ℂ] H)}\n    {A : H →L[ℂ] H} (hT : StronglyTendsto l T A) (B : H →L[ℂ] H) :\n\n### reviews/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann-closeout.md\n# P49A closeout review — strong-operator closed concrete von Neumann algebras\n\n## Decision\n\n**Status: proved at the stated shared-infrastructure scope; queue may advance.**\n\nThe completed Aristotle project was downloaded as\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-strong-operator-closed-von-neumann.tar.gz`\n(SHA-256 `eb1bd6ddf17213aaf2ba0062f0fe7ba5b0851f4a46eff6ea655801bb3f70d56e`)\nand extracted, without building or fetching dependencies, at\n`aristotle_responses/P49A-extracted/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49a-p0kpdbli_aristotle/`.\n\nOnly the packet-authorized module\n`AristotleCandidates/StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann.lean` was integrated\ninto the live project. Its SHA-256 is\n`dfb39289d895c16400e05145112320a42e6d1b61736859edbba153d02df0571a`\nin both the quarantine snapshot and live project. The archive and extraction\nremain raw response records. No manuscript file was modified.\n\n## Exact declarations and assumptions\n\nFor `H` with `[NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℂ H]`, the module\ndefines the SOT synonym `StrongOperator.SOT H`, the pointwise predicate\n`StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto`, and `StrongOperator.IsStronglyClosed`.\nThe exact core theorems are:\n\n- `StrongOperator.stronglyTendsto_iff_tendsto_sot` and\n  `StrongOperator.tendsto_sot_iff_forall_tendsto`;\n- `StrongOperator.mem_centralizer_of_stronglyTendsto` and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_centralizer`;\n- under `[CompleteSpace H]`,\n  `StrongOperator.coe_vonNeumannAlgebra_eq_centralizer`,\n  `StrongOperator.mem_vonNeumannAlgebra_of_stronglyTendsto`, and\n  `StrongOperator.isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra`;\n- `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.const_mul`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_const`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_bounded`,\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.mul_of_norm_le`, and\n  `StrongOperator.StronglyTendsto.compress`.\n\nThe only analytic assumptions are the standard complex inner-product-space\nstructure, and completeness precisely where Mathlib's concrete\n`VonNeumannAlgebra H` requires it. The joint-product theorem explicitly\nrequires a uniform norm bound on its left family. No analytic conclusion is a\nstructure field or axiom.\n\n## Acceptance review\n\n| Classification | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| proved | All four packet conclusions are proved: SOT/net equivalence; strong closedness of arbitrary commutants; strong closedness of concrete von Neumann algebras using `M = M''`; and fixed-side plus uniformly bounded joint product stability. |\n| partial | None within the stated P49A infrastructure target. |\n| blocked | Nothing blocks the stated gate. The analytic double-commutant theorem and Kaplansky density remain separate P49B/P49C work. |\n| failed | None. |\n\nThe mathematical target is met at its stated scope. In particular,\n`isStronglyClosed_vonNeumannAlgebra` is a closure theorem for an already\ngiven Mathlib concrete von Neumann algebra; it does not identify the strong\nclosure of an arbitrary star subalgebra with its bicommutant.\n\n## Plan alignment\n\n- **Package and lane:** P49A, Lane shared.\n- **Predecessors:** P48 was previously integrated and locally audited. The\n  candidate imports only the locally present supporting module\n  `AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore`; it imports no P49B, P49C,\n  P50, or later package.\n- **Permitted gate:** discharged: commutants and therefore Mathlib concrete\n  von Neumann algebras are closed under strong-operator limits.\n- **Forbidden downstream claims:** respected. No double-commutant equality\n  with a strong closure, Kaplansky density, corner trace, faithfulness,\n  finiteness, fullness, or type classification is asserted.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann` — passed.\n- `lake build AristotleCandidates.BicommutantVonNeumannCore AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower AristotleCandidates.StrongOperatorClosedVonNeumann Formalization` — passed.\n- `lake build` — passed in the already-built live project.\n- `lake env lean /dev/stdin` with `#print axioms` for all four core\n  conclusions and the compression corollary — each reports only\n  `propext`, `Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound`.\n- Placeholder/forbidden-declaration scan of the candidate — no executable\n  `sorry`, `admit`, user `axiom`, `opaque`, `unsafe`,\n  `implemented_by`, or `native_decide` declaration. Search hits occur only\n  in the file's explicit negative-scope documentation.\n- Quarantine/live byte comparison, SHA-256 comparison, and `git diff --check`\n  — passed.\n\n## Adversarial review\n\nNo acceptance-blocking finding. The review checked that the centralizer proof\npasses the commutation equation pointwise through the two strong limits; that\nthe concrete von Neumann result uses only its defining bicommutant equality;\nand that the product proof has the required uniform norm bound on the left\nfactor. The remaining risk is exactly the deliberately deferred P49B/P49C\nanalytic identification and density work; compilation and axiom inspection do\nnot establish those results.\n\n## Cleanup and worktree state\n\nKept intentionally: the integrated P49A candidate, its ignored quarantine\narchive and extraction, and this closeout review. No commit, push, manuscript\nchange, dependency update, archive build, or dependency fetch was performed\nlocally. The new candidate and review are the only working-tree changes from\nthis closeout.\n--- task log ---\nID                                   CREATED              NAME                           STATUS         \n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n77f02cc4-2096-4f34-a09d-47c9a693c2d6 1 hour ago           # Autonomous proof-developm... COMPLETE       \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
