{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba sources/manuscript/main.tex | sed -n '1100,1208p' && printf '\\\\n--- live archive candidate source-tree diff ---\\\\n' && diff -u --label live --label quarantine /dev/null aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean | sed -n '1,100p' && printf '\\\\n--- import dependency forbidden markers ---\\\\n' && rg -n 'import AristotleCandidates\\\\.(P|StrongOperator|VonNeumannBicommutant|Kaplansky|NormalFaithful|FullFinite)' aristotle_responses/P49-quarantine/aristotle-stabilizer_two_lane_p49-gizp5x2z_aristotle/AristotleCandidates/FiniteCornerTrace.lean || true\"","aggregated_output":"  1100\t\\end{proof}\n  1101\t\n  1102\t\\begin{proof}[Proof of Lemma \\ref{lema:proj_inequality}]\n  1103\t    Since by Eq. \\eqref{eq:rho-compatibility} $\\r_{\\G_n} = \\Tr_{\\G_{n+1} \\setminus \\G_{n}} \\r_{\\G_{n+1}}$, the previous lemma implies\n  1104\t    \\begin{equation}\n  1105\t        s(\\r_{\\G_n}) \\otimes \\id_{\\G_{n+1} \\setminus \\G_{n}} \\geq s(\\r_{\\G_{n+1}}).\n  1106\t    \\end{equation}\n  1107\t    By the defintion of $P_{\\G_n}$ we have $s(\\r_{\\G_n})=P_{\\G_n}$. Thus the canonical inclusions give\n  1108\t    $P_n \\geq P_{n+1}$, and since\n  1109\t    the GNS representation is a $\\ast$-homomorphism and therefore also preserves\n  1110\t    inequalities, the original statement follows.\n  1111\t\\end{proof}\n  1112\t\n  1113\tWe thus have\n  1114\t\\begin{lemma}\\label{lem:q_exists}\n  1115\t    The sequence $p_n$ has a strong limit $q$, $q \\in \\cM_\\G$ and we have \n  1116\t    \\begin{equation}\\label{eq:proj_stabilizer}\n  1117\t        q \\ket{\\W} = \\ket{\\W}.\n  1118\t    \\end{equation}    \n  1119\t\\end{lemma}\n  1120\t\\begin{proof}\n  1121\t    By \\cite[I.5.1.3]{Blackadar} a decreasing net of projections in $\\cB(\\cH)$ has\n  1122\ta strong limit, i.e.\n  1123\t\\begin{equation}\n  1124\t    p_n \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}} q\n  1125\t\\end{equation}\n  1126\tfor some $q$. Since $M_\\G$ is a von Neumann algebra, by the bicommutant theorem\n  1127\t\\cite[I.9.1.2]{Blackadar} it is strongly closed. Since $p_n \\in M_\\G, \\forall\n  1128\tn$ we have that its strong limit also belong to $M_\\G$, so that $q \\in M_\\G$.\n  1129\tTo proof $q \\ket{\\W} = \\ket{\\W}$ we consider the vector \n  1130\t\\begin{equation}\n  1131\t    v = (1-q) \\ket{\\W}\n  1132\t\\end{equation}\n  1133\tand show that $\\norm{v} = 0$. Since $q$ is the strong limit, we know that \n  1134\t\\begin{equation}\n  1135\t    v_n = (1-p_n) \\ket{\\W}\n  1136\t\\end{equation}\n  1137\tconverges to $v$ in norm. But\n  1138\t\\begin{equation}\n  1139\t    \\norm{v_n}^2 = \\bra{\\W}(1-p_n)^2 \\ket{\\W} = \\bra{\\W}(1-p_n)\\ket{\\W} = \\w(1)\n  1140\t    - \\w(P_n).\n  1141\t\\end{equation}\n  1142\tFurthermore,\n  1143\t\\begin{equation}\n  1144\t    \\w(P_n) = \\Tr_{\\G_n}(\\r_{\\G_n}P_n)\n  1145\t    = \\Tr_{\\G_n}(\\r_{\\G_n}) = 1,\n  1146\t\\end{equation}\n  1147\tso that $\\norm{v_n}^2 = 0$ and thus $v_n = 0$, which implies by\n  1148\tnorm-convergence that $v = 0$, which implies Eq. \\eqref{eq:proj_stabilizer}.\n  1149\t\\end{proof}\n  1150\tWe now want to embark on the proof that for the algebra $qM_\\G q$, the state\n  1151\t$\\ket{\\W}$ is a finite tracial state i.e.\n  1152\t\\begin{theorem}\n  1153\t    The functional\n  1154\t    \\begin{equation}\n  1155\t        \\tau_q(x) = \\bra{\\W} x \\ket{\\W},\\quad x \\in q M_\\G q\n  1156\t    \\end{equation}\n  1157\t    is a faithful normal tracial state.\n  1158\t\\end{theorem}\n  1159\tWe will do so by proving it for increasingly larger subalgebras. \n  1160\t\n  1161\t\\begin{lemma}\\label{lem:finite-trace}\n  1162\t    For every $a,b \\in \\cU_{\\Gamma,\\mathrm{fin}}$,\n  1163\t\\begin{equation}\\label{eq:local_trace}\n  1164\t  \\tau_q\\bigl((qaq)(qbq)\\bigr)\n  1165\t  =\n  1166\t  \\tau_q\\bigl((qbq)(qaq)\\bigr).\n  1167\t\\end{equation}\n  1168\t\\end{lemma}\n  1169\t\n  1170\t\\begin{proof}\n  1171\tChoose $m$ large enough such that $a,b\\in\\cU_{\\G_m}$, and choose\n  1172\t$\\widetilde a,\\widetilde b\\in\\cA_{\\G_m}$ with\n  1173\t$a=\\pi_\\w(\\widetilde a)$ and $b=\\pi_\\w(\\widetilde b)$. For every $n\\geq m$,\n  1174\tregard $\\widetilde a$ and $\\widetilde b$ as elements of $\\cA_{\\G_n}$. Then\n  1175\t\\begin{align}\\label{eq:local_state}\n  1176\t  \\bra{\\W}p_nap_nbp_n\\ket{\\W}\n  1177\t  &= \\omega\\bigl(P_n\\widetilde aP_n\\widetilde bP_n\\bigr) \\\\\n  1178\t  &= \\frac{|\\cG_{\\cS,\\G_n}|}{2^{|\\G_n|}}\n  1179\t  \\Tr_{\\G_n}\\bigl(P_n\\widetilde aP_n\\widetilde bP_n\\bigr).\n  1180\t\\end{align}\n  1181\tSince\n  1182\t\\begin{equation}\n  1183\t  P_n\\widetilde aP_n\\widetilde bP_n\n  1184\t  =(P_n\\widetilde aP_n)(P_n\\widetilde bP_n),\n  1185\t\\end{equation}\n  1186\tcyclicity of the finite-dimensional matrix trace gives\n  1187\t\\begin{equation}\n  1188\t  \\Tr_{\\G_n}\\bigl(P_n\\widetilde aP_n\\widetilde bP_n\\bigr)\n  1189\t  =\\Tr_{\\G_n}\\bigl(P_n\\widetilde bP_n\\widetilde aP_n\\bigr).\n  1190\t  \\label{eq:local_traciality}\n  1191\t\\end{equation}\n  1192\t\n  1193\tSince it is a set of projections, the sequence $(p_N)$ is uniformly bounded and\n  1194\tconverges strongly to $q$. Since $a,b$ are bounded operators, the set of\n  1195\toperators $p_n a p_n, p_n b p_n$ is uniformly\n  1196\tbounded by $\\max(\\norm{a},\\norm{b})< \\infty$.\n  1197\tBy \\cite[I.3.2.1]{Blackadar} multiplication is jointly strongly continuous on bounded sets, so\n  1198\t\\begin{equation}\n  1199\t  p_Nap_Nbp_N\n  1200\t  \\xrightarrow{\\mathrm{s}}\n  1201\t  qaqbq.\n  1202\t\\end{equation}\n  1203\tThe same holds with $a$ and $b$ interchanged.  Taking the limit\n  1204\tof~\\eqref{eq:local_state} and using~\\eqref{eq:local_traciality}\n  1205\tproves~\\eqref{eq:local_trace}.\n  1206\t\\end{proof}\n  1207\tNow that we have traciality on simple operators, we can study it on \n  1208\t\n\n--- live archive candidate source-tree diff ---\n--- live\n+++ quarantine\n@@ -0,0 +1,763 @@\n+import Mathlib\n+import AristotleCandidates.CenterFiniteProjectionCore\n+import AristotleCandidates.GeneralLatticeProjectionTower\n+import AristotleCandidates.ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel\n+import AristotleCandidates.DensityPartialTrace\n+\n+/-!\n+# P49 — finite-stage trace cyclicity and the compressed quasi-local corner\n+\n+**Source basis:** `main.tex:1196-1335` (equation `eq:local_traciality`, the\n+strong-limit passage after it, Lemma `lem:cstar_trace`, and the *statement* of\n+the compressed functional `tau_q(x) = <Omega| x |Omega>`).\n+\n+**Plan alignment.**  Package `P49`, lane `G`.  Predecessors used: `P47`\n+(`CenterFiniteProjectionCore`) and `P48` (`GeneralLatticeProjectionTower`),\n+both already integrated.  The gate discharged here is *finite-stage cyclicity*\n+of the compressed vector functional together with its *compatible limit* on the\n+compressed quasi-local C⋆-algebra, keeping the finite codespace density data\n+explicit.\n+\n+**Forbidden downstream claims, not made anywhere in this file.**  No normality,\n+no faithfulness on the von Neumann corner, no fullness of `q`, no finiteness of\n+`q`, no global trace or weight on `M_Gamma`, and no type-III exclusion.  In\n+particular nothing below mentions Kaplansky density, the double commutant, or\n+`q M_Gamma q`: the tracial identity is proved exactly on the *norm-closed*\n+compressed quasi-local C⋆-algebra, which is the furthest the existing\n+completion interfaces support.\n+\n+## What is constructed and proved\n+\n+### The compressed functional\n+\n+* `tauVec Ω : (H →L[ℂ] H) →L[ℂ] ℂ`, `x ↦ ⟪Ω, x Ω⟫` — the vector functional\n+  `tau_q` of the manuscript, packaged as a *continuous* linear functional, so\n+  the manuscript's \"`tau_q` is bounded, hence norm continuous\" step is a\n+  structural fact rather than an assumption.\n+* `compressL q`, `x ↦ q x q` — the compression map, again continuous linear.\n+* `cornerTau q Ω = tauVec Ω ∘ compressL q` — the compressed functional, with\n+  `cornerTau_star_mul_self` (positivity) and `cornerTau_one` (normalization,\n+  under `q Ω = Ω`, `‖Ω‖ = 1`).\n+* `compressL_mem_corner` — the compression lands in the corner `q M q` of P47.\n+  This is the only P47 interface used, and no property of that corner is\n+  invoked.\n+\n+### Explicit finite codespace density data\n+\n+* `stabilizerCodeDensity` — the finite codespace density matrix\n+  `rho = (trace P)⁻¹ • P` attached to the finite group-average code projection\n+  `P` of `AristotleCandidates.groupAverage`, with\n+  `trace_stabilizerCodeDensity` (`Tr rho = 1`),\n+  `posSemidef_stabilizerCodeDensity` (`rho ≥ 0`) and\n+  `stabilizerCodeDensity_eq_smul` (`rho = (|G| / dim) • P`, the manuscript's\n+  normalization `rho_{Gamma_n} = |G_{S,Gamma_n}| 2^{-|Gamma_n|} P_{Gamma_n}`).\n+* `trace_density_sandwich_comm` — the finite-dimensional cyclicity\n+  `Tr(rho P a P b P) = Tr(rho P b P a P)` for `rho = c • P` and `P` idempotent.\n+  This is exactly `main.tex` eq. `eq:local_traciality`.\n+\n+### The finite-stage system and its limit\n+\n+* `FiniteCodespaceSystem Ω ι` — the explicit finite-stage data: stage star\n+  representations `pi n` of the finite matrix algebras, idempotent hermitian\n+  code projections `codeProj n`, densities `density n = weight n • codeProj n`\n+  of trace one, and the vector-state identity\n+  `⟪Ω, pi n x Ω⟫ = Tr(density n * x)`.\n+* `FiniteCodespaceSystem.stageProj` (`p n`), proved to be a star projection,\n+  with `stageProj_apply_self` (`p n Ω = Ω`, the finite-stage form of the\n+  manuscript's `‖(1 - p_n)Ω‖ = 0` computation) and `stage_cyclic`\n+  (finite-stage cyclicity of the vector state).\n+* `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem` — the same data with stage inclusions, from\n+  which `trace_density_incl` (the *functional* form of the density\n+  compatibility `rho_n = Tr_{Gamma_{n+1} \\ Gamma_n} rho_{n+1}`) and\n+  `range_pi_monotone` are derived.\n+* `tendsto_tauVec_sandwich` — the strong-limit passage\n+  `⟪Ω, p_n a p_n b p_n Ω⟫ → ⟪Ω, q a q b q Ω⟫`.  The manuscript invokes joint\n+  strong continuity of multiplication on bounded sets; because `q Ω = Ω` the\n+  same conclusion is obtained here from `p_n → q` strongly alone, which is a\n+  strictly weaker input.\n+* `CornerTracialOn` and `CornerTracialOn.closure` — the norm-density extension\n+  (`main.tex` Lemma `lem:cstar_trace`).\n+* `cornerTracialOn_quasilocalCStarAlgebra` — the tracial identity on the\n+  concrete quasi-local C⋆-algebra of `ConcreteQuasilocalCStarModel`.\n+* `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem.finite_corner_trace` — the packaged\n+  conditional theorem.\n+* `qubitPureMixedDensity_trace_succEmbedding` — a check that the project's own\n+  explicit finite-stage densities satisfy the compatibility shape used by\n+  `CompatibleFiniteCodespaceSystem`.\n+* `sanitySystem`, `sanitySystem_isDecreasingProjTower` — a concrete model\n+  satisfying every field and premise, so the conditional theorem is not\n+  vacuous.\n+\n+## Auxiliary assumptions (all explicit Lean fields or premises, no axioms)\n+\n+1. `FiniteCodespaceSystem`: the finite-stage star representations `pi n`, the\n+   idempotent hermitian matrices `codeProj n`, the *scalar-multiple* form\n+   `density n = weight n • codeProj n` of the finite codespace densities, their\n+   normalization `Tr(density n) = 1`, and the vector-state identity\n+   `⟪Ω, pi n x Ω⟫ = Tr(density n * x)`.  The last field is the GNS input; it is\n\n--- import dependency forbidden markers ---\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
